### ClaimFlow API — manual request collection
### Works with VS Code's "REST Client" extension or JetBrains' built-in HTTP client.
### Everything goes through the gateway on :5100 — never call the service ports directly from the browser/UI,
### they skip authentication enforcement and CORS that the gateway provides.
###
### Flow: run "Login" first, copy the token into @token below, then run anything else.

@gateway = http://localhost:5100/api
@token = PASTE_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Demo accounts (public — no token needed). Same password for everyone.
GET {{gateway}}/identity/demo-users

### 2. Login as a claimant
# @name loginClaimant
POST {{gateway}}/identity/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mei.tan@claimflow.demo",
  "password": "Demo@123"
}

### 3. Login as a claims officer (authority: USD 10,000)
# @name loginOfficer
POST {{gateway}}/identity/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "arjun.nair@claimflow.demo",
  "password": "Demo@123"
}

### 4. Login as the claims manager (unlimited authority)
# @name loginManager
POST {{gateway}}/identity/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sofia.reyes@claimflow.demo",
  "password": "Demo@123"
}

### 5. Who am I?
GET {{gateway}}/identity/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ───────────────────────── Claimant journey ─────────────────────────

### 6. My policies (claimant)
GET {{gateway}}/policies/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Submit a claim (claimant). Use a policy number from #6.
POST {{gateway}}/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policyNumber": "SG-MTR-100201",
  "type": "Motor",
  "incidentDate": "2026-10-20",
  "incidentLocation": "PIE near Toa Payoh exit",
  "description": "Another car merged into my lane and scraped the whole passenger side.",
  "claimedAmount": 4200,
  "motor": {
    "vehicleRegistration": "SLX 4821 P",
    "thirdPartyInvolved": true,
    "injuryInvolved": false,
    "policeReportNumber": null,
    "drivable": true
  }
}

### 8. My claims (claimant)
GET {{gateway}}/claims/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. One claim's detail — replace {id} with an id from #8
GET {{gateway}}/claims/{id}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Reply to an officer's information request — replace {id} and {requestId}
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/information-requests/{requestId}/respond
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "response": "Photo attached via email, workshop estimate is SGD 3,800."
}

### 11. Withdraw a claim
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/withdraw
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Sorted it out privately with the other party."
}


### ───────────────────────── Claims officer journey ─────────────────────────

### 12. The unassigned queue (most urgent, then oldest)
GET {{gateway}}/claims/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12b. Queue filtered by market / type / priority
GET {{gateway}}/claims/queue?market=SG&type=Motor&priority=Urgent
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Pick up a claim — replace {id}
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. My open work
GET {{gateway}}/claims/my-work
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 15. Request information from the claimant
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/request-information
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "Could you upload the repair quotation or a clear photo of the damage?"
}

### 16. Record an assessment
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/assess
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assessedLoss": 4000,
  "coveredPercent": 100,
  "notes": "Verified against the workshop estimate."
}

### 17. Approve (fails with 422 AUTHORITY_LIMIT if above the officer's limit — try with a large assessedLoss in #16)
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "notes": "Within policy terms."
}

### 18. Decline a claim instead
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "The damage is the result of gradual wear and tear, which is excluded under your policy wording."
}

### 19. Issue payment (after approval)
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/settle
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "paymentReference": ""
}

### 20. Add an internal note (never shown to the claimant)
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Spoke to the workshop — estimate looks consistent with the photos."
}

### 21. Search / browse all claims (staff)
GET {{gateway}}/claims?status=Assessed&page=1&pageSize=25
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 22. Reassign a claim to another officer (manager only) — replace {id}
POST {{gateway}}/claims/{id}/assign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "officerId": "o-002"
}

### 23. Staff directory (for the assign picker)
GET {{gateway}}/identity/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ───────────────────────── Notifications ─────────────────────────

### 24. My notifications
GET {{gateway}}/notifications?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 25. Unread count
GET {{gateway}}/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 26. Mark all read
POST {{gateway}}/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ───────────────────────── Reporting (manager / staff) ─────────────────────────

### 27. Manager overview (exposure, SLA breaches, approval rate…) — manager only
GET {{gateway}}/reports/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 28. Liability exposure by market / type / status — manager only
GET {{gateway}}/reports/exposure
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 29. Status breakdown — staff
GET {{gateway}}/reports/status-breakdown
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 30. Officer workload & performance — staff
GET {{gateway}}/reports/workload
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 31. 14-day submitted/decided/settled trend — staff
GET {{gateway}}/reports/trend?days=14
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 32. Claims past their SLA — staff
GET {{gateway}}/reports/sla-breaches
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 33. Recently consumed events (proves the event pipeline is live) — staff
GET {{gateway}}/reports/events/recent?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ───────────────────────── Platform ─────────────────────────

### 34. Aggregated health of every service, plus the active messaging provider (Http | Kafka)
GET {{gateway}}/system/health

### 35. Individual service health (bypassing the gateway, for debugging only)
GET http://localhost:5103/health
